I'm not 100% sure why this is happening (it seems like an indexing translation problem between the two languages), but I am pretty sure this is the solution.

If you try and create a custom metric like this:
```
K <- backend()
metric_mse <- function(y_true, y_pred) {
  return(K$mean(K$square(y_pred + -y_true), axis = 1))
}
```

you will get:
```
 Error in py_call_impl(callable, dots$args, dots$keywords) : 
  RuntimeError: Evaluation error: TypeError: Value passed to parameter 'reduction_indices' has DataType float32 not in list of allowed values: int32, int64. 
```

To hot fix you need to cast the axis
```
K <- backend()
metric_mse <- function(y_true, y_pred) {
  return(K$mean(K$square(y_pred + -y_true), axis = 1L))
}
```

It would be great if the types "just worked"

